{"event_type":"review","id":"9705002de3b96a2d2fe3916c081f4dca39bd85c5414ac5f0c423e9e2cf115928","occurred_at":"2026-11-06T12:52:17Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/352bf45d1a668cf048cb50d086377ac9de827ceda7327f34288b5509cbabf326","sha256":"352bf45d1a668cf048cb50d086377ac9de827ceda7327f34288b5509cbabf326"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8289da1c223c51c52e1ac56f07c3ffa258697c83199377363168024e4b4da562","sha256":"8289da1c223c51c52e1ac56f07c3ffa258697c83199377363168024e4b4da562"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/14d67da3c7481dac333966c3fe612f8c5cdb454b79a266bb9c096cb0cc9ff1f9","sha256":"14d67da3c7481dac333966c3fe612f8c5cdb454b79a266bb9c096cb0cc9ff1f9"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/151c81b62d63ebc6e24642d23da654c35e09feed96cb45feda7a7b871f4e2c67","sha256":"151c81b62d63ebc6e24642d23da654c35e09feed96cb45feda7a7b871f4e2c67"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/db65fb38e09af45d1f86db776db2e5489f9e90547f0424d406c2cb1e955503d7","sha256":"db65fb38e09af45d1f86db776db2e5489f9e90547f0424d406c2cb1e955503d7"}],"attempt_id":"ef6b48ab27db89b63188038cb9038afad69aeb868cebead0c38f0762c1ddbb13:0:1","base":"eb52e4ffaf78b0f8e819cad1b20fdc59a9aef713","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"1fd55d1fc9de61dda5251fa2be33faa3924f12b1","body":"**A cherry-pick conflict leaves the run in `publish_failed` and the tick retries it on every pass.**\n\nFor a merged-PR or receipt run (`record['open_pr']` is false), `target` is the current `DEFAULT_REF` tip (Line 231). The worker produced the commits on `record['base']`, which was the tip at enqueue time. If `main` has since changed the same lines, `wt_git(wt, 'cherry-pick', sha)` at Line 241 raises. `harvest` then sets `record['state'] = 'publish_failed'` (Lines 205-208).\n\n`publish_failed` is in the set that `harvest` re-enters (Line 146). Each later tick does the same work again:\n- It re-verifies every FIXED job in a new detached worktree (Lines 172-181), including a `hack_detector` node run.\n- It calls `publish` again. Because no `publication.json` exists yet, the same cherry-pick fails the same way.\n\n`main` only moves forward, so this conflict never clears. Nothing caps or ends the loop. The run also stays in the `('queued', 'ready', 'publish_failed')` set, so `archive_legacy` (Line 381) stays blocked for good.\n\nTreat a conflict against a moved target as a terminal `stale` outcome, the same way the open-PR path handles a non-fast-forward head at Line 233. Keep `publish_failed` for transient remote errors.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         for v in fixed:\n             before = wt_git(wt, 'rev-parse', 'HEAD')\n-            for sha in v['commits']:\n-                wt_git(wt, 'cherry-pick', sha)\n+            try:\n+                for sha in v['commits']:\n+                    wt_git(wt, 'cherry-pick', sha)\n+            except Exception as exc:\n+                record.update(state='stale',\n+                              error='repair does not apply to current target: ' + str(exc)[:200])\n+                return\n             claims = wt_git(wt, 'rev-list', '--reverse', before + '..HEAD').splitlines()\n```\n</details>","id":"6eb3f20867ede8083de1e7ecb9fe42438caccc64d01b5652e179435ace13af7d","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"A cherry-pick conflict leaves the run in `publishfailed` and the tick retries it on every pass."}],"head":"d4f17f6a340cb50c347fb28f113ddfe0fc6c2837","head_tree":"b4ccd79a879cd59b7eca92377c3b119eff95db28","input_scope":[{"blob":"1094a84392eca9e74ae8f14a36928e0e64e0fd73","intervals":[[1,121]],"path":"apps/crq-python/config.json"},{"blob